  "metadata": {
    "kind": "formula",
    "name": "SMART2 risk score",
    "aliases": [
      "SMART risk score",
      "Secondary prevention MACE"
    ],
    "summary": "Estimates 10-year risk of recurrent myocardial infarction, stroke, or vascular death in patients aged 40–80 with established atherosclerotic disease (CAD, CeVD, PAD, and/or AAA).",
    "short_name": "SMART2",
    "time_estimate": "~2 min",
    "subspecialties": [
      "Other"
    ],
    "clinical_pearls": [
      "Requires at least one manifest atherosclerotic disease location (coronary, cerebrovascular, peripheral arterial, or abdominal aortic aneurysm).",
      "Uses the updated SMART2 algorithm (Hageman et al., Eur Heart J 2022) with competing-risk and geographic E/O recalibration across 369,044 external validation patients.",
      "Pitfall — Modest discrimination & regional variation: C-statistics in secondary prevention cohorts vary (~0.60–0.77), and regional recalibration intercepts may not capture local healthcare disparities or modern intensive GDMT (PCSK9i, SGLT2i) lowering contemporary event rates.",
      "Pitfall — Non-European 10-year extrapolation: True 10-year follow-up in external validation was strongest in European cohorts; non-European 10-year projections rely partially on shorter-horizon extrapolation."
    ]
  },
  "references": [
    {
      "id": "hageman-2022-smart2",
      "citation": "Hageman SHJ, McKay AJ, Ueda P, et al. Estimation of recurrent atherosclerotic cardiovascular event risk in patients with established cardiovascular disease: the updated SMART2 algorithm. Eur Heart J. 2022;43(18):1715-1727.",
      "year": 2022,
      "pmid": "35165703",
      "doi": "10.1093/eurheartj/ehac056",
      "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35165703/",
      "category": "primary"
    }
  ],
